    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1044">

                <pb facs="0896" n="780" sameAs="frus:frus1912/pg780"/>

                <head ana="#head_untitled-inferred-from-preceding-sibling-head">[Untitled]</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1912-04-11T15:00:00-05:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">April 11, 1912—3 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Your request for instructions as to informing Americans they should leave
                    Chihuahua received in undated telegram.<anchor n="1" xml:id="d1044-f1"/>
                    Department must depend upon you and Americans themselves in the first instance
                    to decide whether or not local conditions warrant their departure for a place of
                    safety; but it feels that you may make quiet suggestions to Americans to leave
                    as soon and as unobtrusively as possible in case you still believe it
                    necessary.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Huntington Wilson.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d1044-f1" n="1" xml:id="d1044-f1-content">
                <p>See telegram received April 10.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
